=== TASK ===
Round: r7   Operation: specialisation
Problem: #38 038_flux_multi_head_rmsnorm_qk   Target niche: any empty niche   Target band: S
Return 1 candidate(s). Each must follow OUTPUT CONTRACT exactly. Give every candidate a new unique id starting with 'r7-'.
Goal: cut the fixed cost on small inputs (B*S <= 600). On B200 the parent fits 3.2 us fixed + bytes / 7.5 TB/s on small and medium sizes; reaching 2.0 us fixed would add about +0.020 to the score. Write a small-input kernel behind a dispatch:size wrapper that routes every larger size to the parent's kernel with the parent's exact configuration, so the B200 result isolates the change. The best public B200 streaming kernels take about 2.2-2.5 us in total at the smallest sizes, so about 1 us is recoverable; see b200_sota.md section 4 for what they do. Keep the answer focused: one candidate, and say in the card what you think the fixed cost consists of. Slower on B200 than the parent in this band already: d1-os-r8w4-nohint (ldg128/oneshot): +4%; g2-os-r16w8 (ldg128/oneshot): +4%; g2-os-r8w4 (ldg128/oneshot): +3%; g2-tma-r8s3 (tma-tensor/persistent): +34%; g2-tmaws-hb8s4 (tma-tensor/persistent-wstat): +19%; g2-ws-hb16w8s3 (cpasync/persistent-wstat): +10%; r2-ldg256-os-r16 (ldg256/oneshot): +5%; r3-cute-ldg256-os-r16 (ldg256/oneshot): +3%; v028 (ldg128/persistent): +42%; v039 (ldg128/persistent): +19%; v040 (ldg128/oneshot): +77%; v050 (ldg128/oneshot): +134%. Ideas already proposed but not yet measured on B200 (do not repeat them): r1-bulk1d-ring-r16s16 (bulk1d/persistent, cuda_cpp); r2-ldg256-tokblk (ldg256/oneshot, cuda_cpp); r3-os-l2pf-r8w4 (ldg128/oneshot, cuda_cpp); r3-tokblk-s-disp (ldg128/oneshot, triton); r4-cuda-ldg256-token-r2 (ldg256/oneshot, cuda_cpp); r4-cute-ldg256-sw2-disp (ldg256/persistent, cute_dsl); r4-ldg256-wstat-pf2 (ldg256/persistent-wstat, cuda_cpp); r6-gluon-cpasync-os-r16w8-stel (cpasync/oneshot, gluon); r6-ldg256-qkpair-r16 (ldg256/oneshot, cuda_cpp); r6-s-ldef-nc-disp (ldg256/oneshot, cuda_cpp).

